# Engine

Before deep work, read `MEMORY/durable/engine.md`. After lasting discoveries (gotchas, decisions, follow-ups), update that file.

## Boundaries

- Games depend on `wiimaker-core` (+ `wiimaker-host` / `wiimaker-scene` on desktop). They never talk to GX or window backends directly.
- `wiimaker-core`: `App` / `FrameCtx`, `World`, `Transform` / `Sprite` / `Disc` / `Camera`, `DrawList`, `Input`, `Clock`.
- Rendering path: scene hydrate → `World` → `render_world` (or hand-built `DrawList`) → host raster / Wii GX.

## World model (v0)

Unity-shaped store, not a full ECS:

- Named entities (`find_by_name`)
- Components: `Transform`, `Sprite` (texture by `TextureId`), `Disc`, `Camera`
- Do not add archetype queries / systems UI; extend the v0 component set carefully

Sprite textures resolve from cooked `.wpack` names via hydrate `TextureMap` — keep string names in scene JSON, ids only at runtime.

## Game `App` pattern

```rust
// ✅ load scene once, mutate World in update, render via scene helper
let scene = load_scene(...)?;
let world = hydrate(&scene, atlas.map())?;
// update: world.transform_mut(id)
// render: render_world(&world, clear, draw)
```

Gameplay stays in Rust `App` (MonoBehaviour-like). No visual scripting.

## Host vs Wii

- Host: `wiimaker-host` software raster + atlas; `run` stays minifb (fast). Editor uses egui separately.
- Wii: `runtime/wii` C bootstrap calls Rust `wiimaker_game_frame`. Respect MEM1/MEM2 and fixed-function GX limits.
- Assets: cook offline (`wiimaker-assets`). No PNG decode on console. Non-PoT PNGs pad with warning.

## Do / don't

```rust
// ❌ BAD — platform or serde in core
fn draw_sprite_gx(...);
#[derive(Serialize)] struct Scene { ... } // belongs in wiimaker-scene

// ✅ GOOD — IR only
draw.push(DrawCmd::DrawSprite { texture, dest, uv, color });
```
